codex
The `projectToScreen` helper has a real bug: it calls `camera.updateMatrixWorld()`, which resets the camera's world matrix to identity (the camera is attached to the scene, and its transform is set every frame in `syncCamera` — but `updateMatrixWorld()` on the camera alone recomputes `matrixWorld` from the stale `matrix`, wiping the frame's transform). That's why the previous session's projections were wrong and the step-drivers seemed to fail. Let me fix the helper to read the live matrix instead.


exec
/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n "updateMatrixWorld" game.js' in ~/side-projects/games/web/zombie-fps-local-ai
 succeeded in 0ms:
675:  camera.updateMatrixWorld();

